{"id":"VHH__points__points_in_a_sphere","collection":"VHH","category":"points","source_path":"VHH/points/points_in_a_sphere.json","root_names":["VHH::Core::Geometry::points_in_a_sphere"],"counts":{"nodes":91,"connections":150,"values":28,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"This is basically a \"sphrand\" compound, with various controls. It uses math to generate points in a sphere uniformly, then gives you some options for rearranging them to your liking.","documentation_search":"points in a sphere This is basically a \"sphrand\" compound, with various controls. It uses math to generate points in a sphere uniformly, then gives you some options for rearranging them to your liking. Input how many points Number of points you wish to scatter. radius The radius of the sphere. offset the center of the sphere. seed Seed for the random number generator. interpolation The interpolation of the final points (combo port); Off - no interpolation. Ease in - center points are closer, outer points are spread out. Ease out - center points are spread out, outer points are closer. Smoothstep - smoothly interpolates between center and outer points. Exponent - raises the positions to an exponent, to varying effect. exponent When interpolation is set to exponent, this is the exponent it is raised to. Output size The number of points you have scattered, this can be used in a variety of ways. positions The output positions of the scatter. normals Generated normals of the points. The point outwards from the center.","port_names":["exponent","how_many_points","interpolation","normals","offset","positions","radius","seed","size"],"node_types_search":["Core::Array::array_bounds_impl","Core::Array::first_in_array","Core::Constants::one","Core::Constants::pi","Core::Conversion::scalar_to_vector3","Core::Graph::pass","Core::Logic::equal","Core::Logic::if","Core::Math::acos","Core::Math::add","Core::Math::cos","Core::Math::cube_root","Core::Math::divide","Core::Math::length","Core::Math::multip